# sha256 of PlantUML jars `codemap uml --render` may run, one per line:
#   <sha256>  <file name>  <where it was verified against>
#
# `codemap uml` always writes the .puml TEXT, which any PlantUML viewer
# renders; --render runs `java -jar` on a downloaded jar, so it runs only a jar
# whose digest someone has checked against the publisher and pinned here.
#
# Pinned 2026-10-23 by the owner's decision (roadmap item 9): Maven Central's
# plantuml-mit 1.2026.8, the build a signature covers. Re-checked that day
# before pinning (observed, this container): the jar fetched again from Google's
# Maven Central mirror has the sha256 below, its sha1 equals the .sha1 Maven
# publishes, and its .asc is a GOOD signature by C08C...0213 (key fetched again
# from keyserver.ubuntu.com by id). A newer PlantUML is a new line here, after
# the same checks. The two digests seen on 2026-10-16 were reconciled on
# 2026-10-22 (observed, this container):
#   - They are two BUILDS of plantuml-mit 1.2026.8, not two releases: the jars
#     have the same 5812 entries, same sizes and entry timestamps; exactly two
#     classes differ (version/CompilationInfo.class, version/Version.class), in
#     3 bytes each -- an embedded compile time, 2026-09-05T16:46:13.766Z in
#     Maven Central's jar, 15:59:17.045Z in the GitHub release's.
#   - Maven Central's jar (fetched from Google's Maven Central mirror; repo1
#     answered 429): sha1 d19535573bd16fc2150592448a91d164a2163aaa and md5
#     b163a091b04c4688e96b57e5f40c3cb4, both equal to what Maven publishes;
#     its .asc is a GOOD signature by "PlantUML JAR Signing Key", rsa4096
#     C08C 18EE 1706 DB37 8BD9  93C8 0195 86D4 4BD8 0213, which also signed
#     plantuml-mit 1.2023.7, 1.2024.8 and 1.2026.6 on Maven. That key was
#     fetched from keyserver.ubuntu.com by key id; confirming it against a page
#     PlantUML controls was UNMEASURABLE here (plantuml.com is blocked by this
#     environment's proxy).
#       sha256 8a171e8941d1f68f4ec28f5c180a4bf8d54a2cd679348370d4ba59fc9fb910e3
#   - The GitHub release jar: sha1 ef49f4f313d06de6575dcaa67361df432c028048,
#     sha256 3629c9cd017c7f73e6450396eea0040216c7e1eef8473ce33cc1aad469dab2f9;
#     Maven's signature reads BAD against it (it covers the other build), and
#     the release's own digests could not be read (GitHub's API answered 403).
# The GitHub release's build is deliberately NOT pinned: no signature covers it.

8a171e8941d1f68f4ec28f5c180a4bf8d54a2cd679348370d4ba59fc9fb910e3  plantuml-mit-1.2026.8.jar  Maven Central, sha1 as published, GOOD signature by C08C...0213
